1 MX | CLAUDE.md:14 combines instruction-level precedence with an agent duty on contradictions.
  - IA m=MN | Engineering policy lives in the instruction system; a more volatile level may refine but must not contradict a more stable level (level precedence of L0's instruction topology).
  - XW m=M rel=GOV-018,GOV-009 | When two instruction levels contradict each other the agent reports the contradiction instead of choosing a side.
    s: A Level-2 rule contradicts a Level-1 rule while implementing a feature: the oracle has no rule for instruction-level conflicts (GOV-009 covers only SPECIFICATION/CUSTOM_SETTINGS, GOV-018 questionable requests); L0 requires reporting instead of picking one.
2 NN c=M rel=TST-006 | Technique inside a workflow step: making Program visible (e.g. 'public partial class Program;') is a compile-time necessity for WebApplicationFactory<Program> when top-level statements hide it; the 'e.g.' form is illustrative and the step imposes nothing beyond using the TST-006 baseline.
